  "title": "Raspberry Pi autofocus cannot complete with one request per exposure",
  "description": "RPI_AF only queues AfModeAuto/AfTriggerStart for the next exposure; each exposure restarts the camera with a single request, so the scan cannot complete, RPI_AF reports OK immediately and the AF lens position is not read back. An abort or frame timeout also drops a pending trigger. Next: design streaming AF with AfState/LensPosition metadata and test on an autofocus camera (e.g. Camera Module 3).\n\nImported from .factory/findings/active/FND-20261024202957-6bd9-fix-ccd-rpi-001.json (category: functional, blocking: no).",
